NEXT TEST: Test 1, run 8: DM + player script, player stops, on Deepgram
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Why: run 7 gave the Deepgram baseline with the DM alone. Still open: two speakers, a
player stopping, a first-time question, and a first live look at PRs #192 (#188),
#184, #194, #195 (#190), #196, #202, #206 (#107), #207 (#108), #208 (#99), #214
(scene hints), #220 (heard counts), #223 and #226 (name card), and now #241, #244,
#249, #262, #270, #276, #283, #284, #288. Nothing blocks it.
Already confirmed in run 8a: consent carries over, Stop recording me and I consent
again work at once, the download is offered.

Where: cloud test server, Docker Compose, TRANSCRIBER=deepgram (nova-3),
DMBOT_DEBUG_AUDIO=1, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set. Deployed: e299bfc (2026-10-08 18:18 UTC).

Before the test (owner)
  [ ] Tell the server session how many people (1 = DM only, 2 = DM + player, ...);
      paste the matching docs/test-scripts/ script into Discord. If development has
      moved since e299bfc, ask it to redeploy first. Use a steady connection (run 8a
      on bad Wi-Fi got 26% of the audio)
  [ ] Someone who has NOT agreed before (ideally a third account) in voice before
      /dmbot start, for the first-time question
  [ ] Add Auril and Caer-Dineval with /dmbot names -> Add a name (run 7's two misses)
  [ ] Everyone presses I consent (private message, or /consent give) BEFORE speaking
  [ ] At each (( dramatic pause )): mute, count to three, unmute

What to check
  - #188: the transcript channel is only repaired by a /dmbot start. So start and stop
    once from another channel first, then type /dmbot start INSIDE #dmb-transcript-...
    It should work. If it still hangs for the DM (an Administrator), note it
  - The player's request names Deepgram; capture starts only after their yes
  - Lines in #dmb-transcript-... a few seconds after speaking, labelled per speaker,
    no pop-ups (#194); the DM screen stays quiet
  - Stop recording me -> no more lines from that player
  - A player peeking at the DM screen can use /consent revoke there (#190)
  - The DM screen's list of who is recorded changes as people agree or stop (#107)
  - The Stop listening button ends the session like /dmbot stop (#108)
  - Name card (#223, #226): /dmbot names, open Auril, try Fix spelling and Edit other
    names; Remove asks first and Undo brings it back. After the session, its card
    shows "Last heard" (#220)
  - Wait for the script's last line in the transcript channel, then /dmbot stop:
    last words kept and a session summary posted (#202), a download offered (#196),
    and, if DMbot heard names it doesn't know, "Check new names" (#184)
  - Score it (docs/test-scripts/README.md): audio from ears lines, pieces of speech,
    Part 1 of 35 (dm-and-player), Part 2 of 12, whisper, first word after each split
    pause (#121). Note whether Auril and Caer-Dineval are now right (hints help, they
    don't guarantee). Compare with run 7 below
